X-ray Powder Diffraction Structural Analysis (XRPD). A powdered, microcrystalline sample of DMF-solvated NiBDP_ $\underline{{s}}\mathbf{O}_{3}\mathbf{H}$ (NiBDP_ $\mathbf{SO}_{3}\mathbf{H}{\cdot}2\mathbf{D}\mathbf{M}\mathbf{F},$ ) was deposited in the hollow of an aluminum sample holder equipped with a zero-background plate. As the compound is poorly stable at ambient conditions, due to quick solvent release, numerous attempts were preliminary carried out to find proper measurement settings: with our setup, solvent loss was invariably faster than the time scale of the XRPD acquisition. The best compromise between a limited solvent loss and data of sufficient quality to allow a structural analysis was found collecting only in the $6-55^{\circ}2\theta$ range $\langle\Delta2\theta\ =\ 0.02^{\circ}$ , 1 h scan). Data collections were performed on a Bruker AXS D8 Advance diffractometer, equipped with a linear position-sensitive Lynxeye detector, primary beam Soller slits, and Ni-filtered Cu $\mathrm{K}\alpha$ radiation $(\lambda~=~1.5418\mathrm{~\AA~})$ . Generator setting: $40\ \mathrm{kV},$ 40 mA. Standard peak search, followed by indexing with TOPAS,12 allowed the detection of approximate unit cell parameters: monoclinic $P,$ $a=7.52\mathrm{~\AA},$ $b=16.3\dot{2}\dot{\mathrm{~\AA~}},c=17.60\mathrm{~\AA~},\beta=$ $94.17^{\circ}$ , $V=2155.63\mathrm{~}\mathring{\mathrm{A}}_{:}^{3}$ , and $\mathrm{GOF}=17.5\$ . The space group $P2_{\mathrm{1}}/c$ was assigned on the basis of the systematic absence conditions and was later confirmed by a Le Bail refinement. Structure solution was performed by the simulated annealing technique, as implemented in TOPAS, using for $\mathbf{H}_{2}\mathbf{BDP\_}\mathbf{SO}_{3}\mathbf{H}$ and DMF rigid, idealized models. The final refinement was carried out by the Rietveld method, maintaining the rigid bodies introduced at the structure solution stage. The background was modeled by a polynomial function of the Chebyshev type. One, refined, isotropic thermal parameter was assigned to the metal atoms, augmented by $2.0\mathrm{~\AA~}^{2}$ for lighter atoms.
For the other two structures reported below (the NiBD$\mathbf{P_{-}}\mathbf{SO_{3}H\cdot D M F}$ and NiBDP_ $\mathbf{\underline{{so}}_{3}H}$ species), an identical procedure was applied to diffractograms collected at 90 and $250^{\circ}\mathrm{C},$ for which the same apparatus used for the variable-temperature experiments was adopted. For these experiments, overnight data collections were performed in the ranges $6{-}70^{\circ}$ and $7-35^{\circ}2\theta$ $\ \langle\Delta2\theta\ =\ 0.02^{\circ},$ , respectively. The final Rietveld refinement plots for the three compounds are shown in Figure S1.
